  "question": {
    "text": "Two particles are projected vertically upwards from the surface of the earth with velocities <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>&nbsp;respectively. If the maximum heights attained by the two particles are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> respectively, then calculate the ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": ".25",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Loss of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KE</mi><mo>=</mo></math> Gain in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PE</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>mv</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>mgh</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p>CASE I.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>gR</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>mgh</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;...(i)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>mgh</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; ...(ii)</p><p>Solving (i)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; ...(iii)</p><p>Solving (ii)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; ...(iv)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math></p><p>From (iii) and (iv)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p>",
